 "_rhel7_note": "CR-T-12 (2026-09-17, Milo Vance): flags_rhel7.json is now populated from a rootless UBI7 container on saratoga (no RHEL 7 host in the lab; see its _meta.host/container_image_digest). Q20's RAW_DIR_FOR in qa.py is hardcoded to {'8': 'rhel8', '10': 'rhel10'} and was NOT extended to '7' here (out of this task's touch-restriction on qa.py) -- so Q20 does not gate RHEL 7 coverage yet; this coverage['7'] block is recorded for the same reason RHEL 8/10 were recorded and for whoever extends RAW_DIR_FOR next. firewall-cmd is not in this block at all: firewalld is not installable from UBI7's public repos (no matching package), so flags_rhel7.json carries no firewall-cmd flags to measure -- the synopsis-line regex gap that costs RHEL 8/10 their --add-rich-rule coverage (see 'firewall-cmd' rows above and README.md's Content authoring note) is therefore NOT OBSERVABLE on RHEL 7 with this source; it would very likely reproduce byte-for-byte if a real firewalld package/man page were ever read on RHEL 7, since the regex bug is in extract_flags.py's parser, not in anything host-specific. Recorded under the same ratchet owner and date as the rest of this file: Caleb Stone, retires 2026-09-25 -- no separate date was invented for RHEL 7."
}
